  "notes": "Oviedo Cathedral presents three recessed pointed portals and a rose window to the west plaza. The single southern tower rises to a perforated Gothic spire. A tiled nave, chapels and the Cámara Santa exterior connect to the open Museo Catedralicio cloister. The cathedral, single tower and connected museum cloister use mapped building outlines. Smaller roofs and facade ornament are exterior photo reconstructions. The portico is open to the recessed doors. The model depicts the Cámara Santa exterior and the cloister arcade. Interior rooms, relics and carved figures use exterior viewing scale or are outside the model scope.",
